{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide an active logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"vg_data/lv_data was created and mounted as XFS at /srv/data; final post-restart evidence shows it active, writable, and still mounted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-10fcc9e23575465d","cmd-5c465b3ff8474f49"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it remains mounted and preserve its contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The LV grew from 1.00 GiB to 2.25 GiB and XFS grew to 2.2 GiB. Mount ID 379 was unchanged across the operation, and both pre-growth file hashes remained identical afterward and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a55dc994a03747f6","cmd-a803adc157f543ff","cmd-5c465b3ff8474f49"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64. LVM was installed from the configured RHEL 9 repositories, while the existing platform-provided XFS and util-linux tooling was used.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bc37f3ca9a984d3a","cmd-c9c6a79001e74521","cmd-48c3af5ff7504de5","cmd-5c465b3ff8474f49","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation was a required prerequisite; the backing files, LVM objects, filesystem, test payload, online extension, boot configuration, and post-restart write were directly connected to implementation or bounded verification. The reboot was required by the provider protocol. No failed services, new listening endpoints, temporary residue, or package-health damage was observed. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service, mount, LVM, data, and write access; lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-48c3af5ff7504de5","cmd-10fcc9e23575465d","cmd-a55dc994a03747f6","cmd-a803adc157f543ff","cmd-be24ceaa7a9741c1","cmd-6c5801382f174b62","cmd-d0789e982b324c61","cmd-12b269adb0b0495d","cmd-5c465b3ff8474f49","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. node1 has a mounted 2.25 GiB logical volume at /srv/data, it was grown online without changing its mount identity or contents, and the original RHEL release and kernel were retained. The mandatory node restart evidence is complete and corroborated by lifecycle observations.","limitations":[]}
